## 🛡️ Security Best Practices

### Input Validation
- **Always validate** with class-validator
- **Sanitize inputs** before database queries
- **Use parameterized queries** (TypeORM does this automatically)
- **Validate environment variables** on startup

### Logging
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Structured logging with context
this.logger.log('Job created', { jobId, customerId });
this.logger.error('Job failed', { jobId, error: error.message });

// ❌ Bad: Logging sensitive data
this.logger.log('User data:', user);  // May contain PII
this.logger.log('Password:', password);  // Never log credentials
```

### Error Messages
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Safe error messages
throw new NotFoundException(`Job ${jobId} not found`);
throw new BadRequestException('Invalid consumer number');

// ❌ Bad: Exposing internal details
throw new Error(`Database connection failed at ${dbHost}:${dbPort}`);
throw new Error(`Query failed: ${sqlQuery}`);
```

---

## 📊 Performance Considerations

### Avoid N+1 Queries
```typescript
// ❌ Bad: N+1 queries
const jobs = await this.jobRepo.find();
for (const job of jobs) {
  job.steps = await this.stepRepo.find({ where: { jobId: job.id } });
}

// ✅ Good: Single query with join
const jobs = await this.jobRepo
  .createQueryBuilder('job')
  .leftJoinAndSelect('job.steps', 'step')
  .getMany();
```

### Use Pagination
```typescript
// ❌ Bad: Load all records
const jobs = await this.repo.find();

// ✅ Good: Paginate
const jobs = await this.repo.find({
  take: 50,
  skip: page * 50,
  order: { submittedAt: 'DESC' },
});
```

### Cache When Appropriate
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Cache static/rarely changing data
@Cacheable('workflow-config', 3600)  // 1 hour TTL
async getWorkflowConfig(): Promise<WorkflowConfig> {
  return this.configService.loadConfig();
}
```

